You are working on Sapiens, a Next.js 16 (App Router, React 19, TypeScript) app styled with Tailwind 4.

Layers, from the bottom up: tokens (`src/app/globals.css` `@theme`) → semantic tokens (`:root`/`.dark` and `@theme inline`, used as `bg-surface`, `text-fg-muted`, `border-edge`, `bg-accent`) → components (`src/components`: `ui/` primitives, `shell/` site frame, then domain folders) → screens (`src/app`). Pages load data on the server and compose components; logic lives in `src/lib`.

Rules
- Server components by default; add `'use client'` only where state, effects or browser APIs are needed.
- Use the semantic tokens, never raw zinc/crimson classes with `dark:` variants, except for one-off accents.
- Reuse `ui/` primitives (Button, LinkButton, Card, Field, Badge, Sheet, Modal, Alert, Latex, Html) before writing markup.
- KaTeX runs on the server (`src/lib/content`); the browser loads it only for the chat.
- Metadata through `pageMetadata()` and structured data through `src/lib/seo/jsonld` + `<JsonLd>`.
- Page files export only Next's route config (default, metadata, generateMetadata, revalidate, dynamic); shared helpers go in `src/lib` or `src/components`.
- Route handlers use the helpers in `src/lib/server/http.ts`; sessions come from `src/lib/server/auth.ts`.
- Keep the Playwright suite (`tests/e2e`) passing on desktop and phones; ids and accessible names used by the tests must stay.
- Write terse, factual comments; no filler.
